        "content": "In the context of AI and data protection, lawfulness refers to the requirement that any processing of personal data by an AI system must be based on a lawful basis. This means that the processing must be done in a way that is allowed by law, such as being necessary for the performance of a task carried out for the public interest or essential for the performance of a contract. The ICO provides guidance on how to ensure lawfulness in AI, including considering an alternative lawful basis if the use of an AI system is integral to the service."
